---
/*
  The real blocker of the most valuable group is the old agency, not the price.
  04-konzept.md section 4.3, page "/switching".
  Hard limit that has to stay in the copy: reading and sorting a contract is
  not legal advice. Same logic as the ban on tax and banking statements in
  appendix A of the closing playbook.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Switching agencies | Wunder"
  description="What happens when you are still signed with another agency, in what order, and where our help ends."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Leaving an agency you are already signed with.</h1>
      <p class="lead">This is the part most people are actually stuck on. It is not the money.</p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>I am so nervous about telling my other agency. You have no idea.</p>
        <p class="caption">
          A typical sentence from these conversations, not a testimonial, quoted without a name.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What we do.</h2>
      <p>
        Send us your current contract and we read it with you. We tell you what the notice period
        says, when your next exit window opens, and what the clause about your content means in
        practice.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is reading and sorting, not legal advice. We are not lawyers and we do not act as
        yours. Where a document needs a legal opinion, we say so and you take it to a lawyer.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not contact your current agency, we do not write to them in your name, and we do not
        ask you to break an agreement you signed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The order things happen in.</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>You apply and say in the form that you are currently under contract, and until when.</li>
        <li>We talk anyway. Nothing about that call obliges you to anything.</li>
        <li>We read your contract and work out the earliest clean exit date.</li>
        <li>
          You give notice yourself, in writing, in the window your contract allows. We do not start
          before that date.
        </li>
        <li>
          We start after your old agreement has ended, with the thirty day starting point measured
          on the day we begin.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        If your contract has no clean exit for another few months, we will tell you that and put a
        date in the calendar instead of talking you into something.
      </p>
      <CtaBlock secondary />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  blockquote {
    margin: 32px 0 0;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  blockquote p:first-child {
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  blockquote p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
